  "body": "First research-only release. NeuroCVguard audits supplied cohort identities, split membership, declared dependence and preprocessing provenance; generates checked grouped splits; runs a controlled participant-level classification baseline with optional nested tuning; and writes offline privacy-projected reports. Five fully synthetic examples are included.\r\n\r\nRepeated observations alone are not leakage. Site separation depends on the stated objective. Unknown upstream preprocessing remains unassessable. Association and differences between evaluation designs do not establish causality. Operational split/evaluation files remain sensitive; projected reports are not guaranteed anonymous. No clinical certification or global leakage-free verdict is provided. Regression, changing longitudinal targets and temporal evaluation are unsupported.\r\n\r\nMaintainer: Alireza Emad. License: BSD-3-Clause. AI-assisted implementation and testing are disclosed in AI_ASSISTANCE.md. The owner accepted the technical outputs for this initial release; the maintainer walkthrough and independent-user exercise remain deferred and unfinished. No independent human scientific validation or external adoption is claimed.\r\n\r\nThe reviewed package files retain all 53 scientific runtime payloads from S16; S17 finalizes owner metadata and release operations. Local verification: 733 tests passed, strict documentation/lint/types, exact archive checks and fresh external wheel installation with source-tree access and networking blocked during the demo.\r\n\r\nSHA256:\r\n- neurocvguard-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl: a40936fb615b86fcb31a0e212bae8075318f1b43bd8950cecebf3a549d5b74b9\r\n- neurocvguard-0.1.0.tar.gz: d12b8ba53bed76293e54bdccb43fb849873a5f6cd89adc3341f6966b0a33020b\r\n\r\nSee docs/release.md and state/handoffs/S17.md for the live publication verification record, known limitations and maintenance follow-ups.\r\n\r\nHosted verification: all six jobs passed on Linux (Python 3.11, 3.12, 3.13 and dependency floor), Windows 3.12 and macOS 3.12, including clean-wheel checks. [CI run](https://github.com/Alireza2177/NeuroCVguard/actions/runs/36299543058). The earlier typing-environment failure and correction are retained in the evidence."
